source "Kconfig.zephyr"

menu "Project-Carl room node"

config CARL_ROOM_SAMPLE_INTERVAL_SEC
    int "Sample + broadcast interval (s)"
    default 30
    range 10 600
    help
        How often the room node samples its sensors and emits a BTHome
        advertisement. Default 30 s is bring-up-friendly; production rooms
        with stable conditions can extend this to 5–10 minutes. T/H/P/lux
        change on minute timescales so faster cadence is wasteful.

config CARL_ROOM_BATTERY_LOW_PCT
    int "Battery-low RGB warning threshold (%)"
    default 15
    range 0 100
    help
        Below this level, a successful broadcast blinks amber instead of
        green so a glance at the node signals "needs a charge" without
        checking the dashboard. Matches the hub's default battery_low_pct
        calibration value for consistency.

endmenu
